IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- s 216A, "Derivative or representative actions" (LAYER 1: the law, objectively; part sgf).
--
-- What is here: who a "complainant" is (s 216A(1)); the application for permission to bring or intervene in an action or arbitration
-- in the company's name (s 216A(2)); what the Court must be satisfied of first, with the 14 days' notice counted (s 216A(3));
-- the interim order where notice is not expedient (s 216A(4)); the orders the Court may make in granting permission, each its own
-- function (s 216A(5)); the District Court rule (s 216A(6)).
--
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.
-- The Court's views (that a person is a proper person, that notice is not expedient) are inputs: judgments the text hands to the Court.
-- Whether the complainant is acting in good faith and whether the action is prima facie in the interests of the company are the kind of
-- judgment the Court makes; they are taken as plain inputs, named for the fact.
-- "The Court" in subsections (3) to (5) is the court that hears the application; where subsection (6) sends the application to a
-- District Court, the text does not say whether those subsections speak of that court (finding 3 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 216A(1): who is a complainant`

-- What the Court has decided about a person who is neither a member nor the Minister (paragraph (c): "any other person who, in the
-- discretion of the Court, is a proper person"). The Court's discretion is its own: the person states what it has done.
DECLARE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court's view of the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has treated the person as a proper person`
    `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person`
    `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not yet decided`

-- (1): "In this section and section 216B, "complainant" means (a) any member of a company; (b) the Minister, in the case of a declared
-- company under Part 9; or (c) any other person who, in the discretion of the Court, is a proper person to make an application under
-- this section." A "means" definition: off the three paragraphs the answer is JUST FALSE, except that where the Court has not yet
-- exercised its discretion on paragraph (c) the text points to a decision not yet made, and the answer is NOTHING (fork F-216A-8).
-- s 216(7) (a transmittee is treated as a member) speaks of "this section", that is s 216 only: it is not applied here (finding 2).
-- src:21784 | 216A.—(1) In this section and section 216B, “complainant”
-- src:21785 | means —
-- src:21787 | (a) any member of a company;
-- src:21789 | (b) the Minister, in the case of a declared company under
-- src:21790 | Part 9; or
-- src:21792 | (c) any other person who, in the discretion of the Court, is a
-- src:21793 | proper person to make an application under this section.
@ref s 216A(1) (src:21784-21793)
GIVEN `the body is a company incorporated under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a declared company under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      view IS A `s 216A(1)(c) the Court's view of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(1) the person is a complainant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a member of the company` AND (`s 4(1) "company" the body is a company` `the body is a company incorporated under this Act` `the body is a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is the Minister` AND `the company is a declared company under Part 9`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF view EQUALS `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has treated the person as a proper person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF view EQUALS `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not yet decided`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(c) any other person who, in the discretion of the Court, is a proper person" -- the Court's discretion has not yet been exercised, so the text does not say
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""complainant" means (a) any member of a company; (b) the Minister, in the case of a declared company under Part 9; or (c) any other person who, in the discretion of the Court, is a proper person" (a "means" definition: none of the three paragraphs holds)

§ `Section 216A(2): the application for permission`

-- What the complainant would do on the company's behalf (subsection (2)).
DECLARE `s 216A(2) what the application is for` IS ONE OF
    `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company`
    `s 216A(2) to bring an arbitration in the name and on behalf of the company`
    `s 216A(2) to intervene in an action to which the company is a party, to prosecute, defend or discontinue it on behalf of the company`
    `s 216A(2) to intervene in an arbitration to which the company is a party, to prosecute, defend or discontinue it on behalf of the company`
    `s 216A(2) for some other purpose`

-- (2): "Subject to subsection (3), a complainant may apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the name
-- and on behalf of the company or intervene in an action or arbitration to which the company is a party for the purpose of
-- prosecuting, defending or discontinuing the action or arbitration on behalf of the company." A grant ("may apply"), limited to a
-- complainant and to the four purposes the text names: outside them the answer is NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1;
-- fork F-216A-1). "Subject to subsection (3)": subsection (3) bars the action itself, not the application; see the bar below.
-- src:21797 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), a complainant may apply to the Court
-- src:21798 | for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the name and on
-- src:21799 | behalf of the company or intervene in an action or arbitration to which
-- src:21800 | the company is a party for the purpose of prosecuting, defending or
-- src:21801 | discontinuing the action or arbitration on behalf of the company.
@ref s 216A(2) (src:21797-21801)
GIVEN `the person is a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 216A(2) what the application is for`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission` MEANS
    IF `the person is a complainant` AND (NOT (purpose EQUALS `s 216A(2) for some other purpose`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a complainant may apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the name and on behalf of the company or intervene in an action or arbitration to which the company is a party" -- the grant names a complainant and four purposes without "only"; a person who is not a complainant, or another purpose, is outside the limit

§ `Section 216A(3): what the Court must be satisfied of first`

-- (3)(a): "the complainant has given 14 days' notice to the directors of the company of the complainant's intention to apply to the Court
-- under subsection (2) if the directors of the company do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action or
-- arbitration". "The directors": every director, and where the company has only one director that director (s 4(10)); fork F-216A-2.
-- "14 days' notice" is counted as "not less than 14 days before the application" (sg-periods P5; the clear-days alternative P7 is the
-- other reading, fork F-216A-3). A condition the text introduces with "unless": not met, JUST FALSE.
-- src:21807 | (3) No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in
-- src:21808 | an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2) unless the
-- src:21809 | Court is satisfied that —
-- src:21811 | (a) the complainant has given 14 days’ notice to the directors
-- src:21812 | of the company of the complainant’s intention to apply to
-- src:21813 | the Court under subsection (2) if the directors of the
-- src:21814 | company do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or
-- src:21815 | discontinue the action or arbitration;
@ref s 216A(3)(a) (src:21807-21815)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors to whom the complainant gave the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice stated the complainant's intention to apply to the Court under section 216A(2) if the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action or arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date the complainant applies to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` MEANS
    IF    (IF `s 4(10) a reference to the directors of the company is a reference to its only director` `the number of directors of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN `the number of directors to whom the complainant gave the notice` AT LEAST 1
           ELSE (`the number of directors of the company` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of directors to whom the complainant gave the notice` EQUALS `the number of directors of the company`))
      AND `the notice stated the complainant's intention to apply to the Court under section 216A(2) if the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action or arbitration`
      AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the notice was given` `the date the complainant applies to the Court` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No action or arbitration may be brought ... unless the Court is satisfied that (a) the complainant has given 14 days' notice to the directors of the company of the complainant's intention to apply" -- a condition introduced with "unless", not met

-- (3)(a), counted from the other end: the latest day on which the notice can be given if the complainant means to apply on a given day.
-- src:21807 | (3) No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in
-- src:21808 | an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2) unless the
-- src:21809 | Court is satisfied that —
-- src:21811 | (a) the complainant has given 14 days’ notice to the directors
-- src:21812 | of the company of the complainant’s intention to apply to
-- src:21813 | the Court under subsection (2) if the directors of the
-- src:21814 | company do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or
-- src:21815 | discontinue the action or arbitration;
@ref s 216A(3)(a) (src:21807-21815)
GIVEN `the date the complainant applies to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 216A(3)(a) the latest day on which the complainant can give the directors notice` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date the complainant applies to the Court` 14 Days

-- (3)(a), counted from this end: the earliest day on which the complainant can apply once the notice has been given.
-- src:21807 | (3) No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in
-- src:21808 | an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2) unless the
-- src:21809 | Court is satisfied that —
-- src:21811 | (a) the complainant has given 14 days’ notice to the directors
-- src:21812 | of the company of the complainant’s intention to apply to
-- src:21813 | the Court under subsection (2) if the directors of the
-- src:21814 | company do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or
-- src:21815 | discontinue the action or arbitration;
@ref s 216A(3)(a) (src:21807-21815)
GIVEN `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 216A(3)(a) the earliest day on which the complainant can apply to the Court` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the notice was given` 14 Days

-- (3)(b): "the complainant is acting in good faith". An "unless" condition, taken as a plain input.
-- src:21807 | (3) No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in
-- src:21808 | an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2) unless the
-- src:21809 | Court is satisfied that —
-- src:21820 | (b) the complainant is acting in good faith; and
@ref s 216A(3)(b) (src:21807-21820)
GIVEN `the complainant is acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(3)(b) the complainant is acting in good faith` MEANS
    IF `the complainant is acting in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No action or arbitration may be brought ... unless the Court is satisfied that ... (b) the complainant is acting in good faith" -- a condition introduced with "unless", not met

-- (3)(c): "it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted, defended
-- or discontinued". An "unless" condition, taken as a plain input.
-- src:21807 | (3) No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in
-- src:21808 | an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2) unless the
-- src:21809 | Court is satisfied that —
-- src:21822 | (c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company
-- src:21823 | that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted,
-- src:21824 | defended or discontinued.
@ref s 216A(3)(c) (src:21807-21824)
GIVEN `it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(3)(c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company` MEANS
    IF `it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No action or arbitration may be brought ... unless the Court is satisfied that ... (c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company" -- a condition introduced with "unless", not met

-- (3) as a whole, named as the bar: "No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in an action or arbitration may be
-- made under subsection (2) unless the Court is satisfied that" (a), (b) and (c). The bar applies where any of the three is not met
-- (JUST TRUE) and does not apply where all three are (JUST FALSE: the "unless" is met). The bar says nothing of the permission
-- itself, which is the Court's under subsection (2); "the Court is satisfied" is encoded as the three facts holding (fork F-216A-4).
-- Outside an action or arbitration under subsection (2) (for instance, at common law) the text says nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:21807 | (3) No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in
-- src:21808 | an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2) unless the
-- src:21809 | Court is satisfied that —
-- src:21811 | (a) the complainant has given 14 days’ notice to the directors
-- src:21812 | of the company of the complainant’s intention to apply to
-- src:21813 | the Court under subsection (2) if the directors of the
-- src:21814 | company do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or
-- src:21815 | discontinue the action or arbitration;
-- src:21820 | (b) the complainant is acting in good faith; and
-- src:21822 | (c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company
-- src:21823 | that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted,
-- src:21824 | defended or discontinued.
@ref s 216A(3) (src:21807-21824)
GIVEN `the action or arbitration is brought, or the intervention is made, under section 216A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors to whom the complainant gave the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice stated the complainant's intention to apply to the Court under section 216A(2) if the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action or arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date the complainant applies to the Court` IS A DATE
      `the complainant is acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(3) the bar on bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the action or arbitration is brought, or the intervention is made, under section 216A(2)`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No action or arbitration may be brought and no intervention in an action or arbitration may be made under subsection (2)" -- a scope limit with no "only"; an action outside subsection (2) is outside the bar
        IF    (`s 216A(3)(a) the complainant has given the directors 14 days' notice` `the number of directors of the company` `the number of directors to whom the complainant gave the notice` `the notice stated the complainant's intention to apply to the Court under section 216A(2) if the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action or arbitration` `the date the notice was given` `the date the complainant applies to the Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
          AND (`s 216A(3)(b) the complainant is acting in good faith` `the complainant is acting in good faith` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
          AND (`s 216A(3)(c) it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company` `it appears to be prima facie in the interests of the company that the action or arbitration be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No action or arbitration may be brought ... unless the Court is satisfied that (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." -- the "unless" condition is met, so the bar does not apply (it does not say the permission is granted)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 216A(4): the interim order where notice is not expedient`

-- (4): "Where a complainant on an application can establish to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as
-- required in subsection (3)(a), the Court may make such interim order as it thinks fit pending the complainant giving notice as
-- required." A "may" gated by "where": SPLIT SITE (ii). Ruling (b) of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05 ("a 'where ...' condition: when
-- it fails the answer is JUST FALSE") is taken as the Guide gives it; the "In short" line on grants points to NOTHING: fork F-216A-5.
-- src:21828 | (4) Where a complainant on an application can establish to the
-- src:21829 | satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as
-- src:21830 | required in subsection (3)(a), the Court may make such interim order
-- src:21831 | as it thinks fit pending the complainant giving notice as required.
@ref s 216A(4) (src:21828-21831)
GIVEN `the complainant has established to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as required in subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(4) the Court may make an interim order pending the complainant giving notice` MEANS
    IF `the complainant has established to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as required in subsection (3)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a complainant on an application can establish to the satisfaction of the Court that it is not expedient to give notice as required in subsection (3)(a), the Court may make such interim order" -- a "may" gated by "where" (split site (ii): the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the other reading is NOTHING, fork F-216A-5)

§ `Section 216A(5): the orders the Court may make in granting permission`

-- (5): "In granting permission under this section, the Court may make such orders or interim orders as it thinks fit in the interests of
-- justice, including (but not limited to) the following". A power with a scope limit ("In granting permission", no "only"): outside it
-- the answer is NOTHING (periods ruling (c) and the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-216A-7). The list is open ("including (but not limited to)").
-- src:21833 | (5) In granting permission under this section, the Court may make
-- src:21834 | such orders or interim orders as it thinks fit in the interests of justice,
-- src:21835 | including (but not limited to) the following:
@ref s 216A(5) (src:21833-21835)
GIVEN `the Court is granting permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF `the Court is granting permission under section 216A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In granting permission under this section, the Court may make such orders or interim orders as it thinks fit" -- a scope limit with no "only"; outside the granting of permission the text does not say

-- (5)(a): "an order authorising the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration".
-- src:21837 | (a) an order authorising the complainant or any other person to
-- src:21838 | control the conduct of the action or arbitration;
@ref s 216A(5)(a) (src:21837-21838)
GIVEN `the Court is granting permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(5)(a) the Court may make an order authorising the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` MEANS
    `s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` `the Court is granting permission under section 216A`

-- (5)(b): "an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised". The named complement
-- is a person who has been authorised under paragraph (a).
-- src:21840 | (b) an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or
-- src:21841 | arbitration by the person so authorised;
@ref s 216A(5)(b) (src:21840-21841)
GIVEN `the Court is granting permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has been authorised to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(5)(b) the Court may make an order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised` MEANS
    IF    `s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` `the Court is granting permission under section 216A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `a person has been authorised to control the conduct of the action or arbitration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the person so authorised" -- a named complement with no "only"; where no person has been authorised, or the Court is not granting permission, the text does not say

-- (5)(c): "an order requiring the company to pay reasonable legal fees and disbursements incurred by the complainant in connection with
-- the action or arbitration". Whether the fees are reasonable is the Court's kind of judgment: a plain input.
-- src:21843 | (c) an order requiring the company to pay reasonable legal
-- src:21844 | fees and disbursements incurred by the complainant in
-- src:21845 | connection with the action or arbitration.
@ref s 216A(5)(c) (src:21843-21845)
GIVEN `the Court is granting permission under section 216A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal fees and disbursements are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal fees and disbursements were incurred by the complainant in connection with the action or arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(5)(c) the Court may make an order requiring the company to pay the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` MEANS
    IF    `s 216A(5) the Court may make the orders or interim orders it thinks fit in the interests of justice` `the Court is granting permission under section 216A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the legal fees and disbursements are reasonable`
      AND `the legal fees and disbursements were incurred by the complainant in connection with the action or arbitration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "reasonable legal fees and disbursements incurred by the complainant in connection with the action or arbitration" -- the order is named for fees that are reasonable and incurred by the complainant; others are outside the limit (the list is open: "including (but not limited to)")

§ `Section 216A(6): the State Courts`

-- (6): "Where the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts, an application for permission under subsection (2)
-- must be made in a District Court." A requirement ("must") gated by "where": when the gate fails the answer is JUST FALSE (periods
-- ruling (b); the provision's own question). It speaks of "the action", not of an arbitration (finding 4).
-- src:21851 | (6) Where the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the
-- src:21852 | State Courts, an application for permission under subsection (2) must
-- src:21853 | be made in a District Court.
@ref s 216A(6) (src:21851-21853)
GIVEN `the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216A(6) the application for permission is required to be made in a District Court` MEANS
    IF `the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the action has been commenced or is to be brought in the State Courts, an application for permission under subsection (2) must be made in a District Court" -- a "where" condition on a requirement, not met (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-216A-6)
